      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vitamin C is a supplement, not a substitute for proper antibiotic treatment when fighting a bacterial infection like a UTI. High doses of Vitamin C are generally safe, but they will not reliably clear a bacterial infection, and your UTI could worsen while you wait. For a potentially serious infection, you need targeted medical care, and I strongly advise finding a low-cost clinic or pharmacy consultation instead of self-treating.",
